---
title: Post card
description: One partial, three layouts. Its context is a Ghost post; it adds the reading time, and flags for featured and members-only posts, by itself.
eyebrow: Component
source: partials/components/post-card.hbs · src/components/post-card.css
---
<h2>Stacked</h2>
{{#example}}
<div class="im-grid-auto" style="--im-grid-min: 14rem">{{#foreach demo.three}}{{> "components/post-card"}}{{/foreach}}</div>
{{/example}}

<h2>With an excerpt</h2>
{{#example}}
<div class="im-grid-auto" style="--im-grid-min: 14rem">{{#foreach demo.three}}{{> "components/post-card" excerpt=true}}{{/foreach}}</div>
{{/example}}

<h2>Cover</h2>
<p>Text over the image, on a gradient. For a featured row.</p>
{{#example}}
<div class="im-grid-auto" style="--im-grid-min: 13rem">{{#foreach demo.three}}{{> "components/post-card" layout="cover"}}{{/foreach}}</div>
{{/example}}

<h2>Row</h2>
<p>Image beside the text; stacks on a phone. For a list view.</p>
{{#example}}
<div class="im-stack">{{#foreach demo.three limit=2}}{{> "components/post-card" layout="row" excerpt=true}}{{/foreach}}</div>
{{/example}}

<h2>Edge cases</h2>
<p>No feature image: the title's initial in Geist Pixel holds the shape, so a grid never has a hole. Members-only: a lock flag.</p>
{{#example}}
<div class="im-grid-auto" style="--im-grid-min: 14rem">
	{{#with demo.noImage}}{{> "components/post-card"}}{{/with}}
	{{#with demo.locked}}{{> "components/post-card"}}{{/with}}
</div>
{{/example}}

<h2>Parameters</h2>
<div class="im-table-scroll">
<table>
	<thead><tr><th>Param</th><th>Values</th></tr></thead>
	<tbody>
		<tr><td><code>layout</code></td><td><code>"cover"</code> · <code>"row"</code> · omit for stacked</td></tr>
		<tr><td><code>excerpt</code></td><td><code>true</code> to show two lines of excerpt</td></tr>
		<tr><td><code>eager</code></td><td><code>true</code> for cards above the fold (skips lazy loading)</td></tr>
	</tbody>
</table>
</div>
<p>The whole card is clickable — the title link's hit area is stretched over it — while the tag and author remain their own links above it. <code>--im-post-card-ratio</code> and <code>--im-post-card-radius</code> adjust the media.</p>
